WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.619
Change management happens in a cycle.

2
00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.930
There is no real stopping point, it is continuously going.

3
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.659
This means that there must be continuous monitoring of that environment.

4
00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.360
So if you or anyone should request a change,

5
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:22.840
it needs to go through the appropriate approvals,

6
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.149
the organization must be prepared for roll back if necessary.

7
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.040
Meaning that if a particular change did not work,

8
00:00:29.049 --> 00:00:31.879
we need to be able to roll back to the legacy system.

9
00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:36.388
While change management is an organization wide process,

10
00:00:36.449 --> 00:00:40.159
it often falls on information security professionals to coordinate

11
00:00:40.168 --> 00:00:43.109
the effort and maybe to provide oversight and governance

12
00:00:43.819 --> 00:00:45.959
depending on the size of the organization.

13
00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:49.560
It may also fall under an it or development area

14
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.270
in organizations that have a quality or risk management department.

15
00:00:53.439 --> 00:00:56.669
It would be a great fit in either of those areas too.

16
00:00:57.319 --> 00:01:01.659
The common theme is that change management acknowledges and incorporates input

17
00:01:01.669 --> 00:01:05.138
from the end users as well as all areas of it,

18
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:09.809
development, information security and most importantly management

19
00:01:09.919 --> 00:01:12.769
to ensure that all changes are properly tested,

20
00:01:12.779 --> 00:01:16.059
approved and communicated prior to being implemented.